  <div class="intro-box">
    <h2>Quick reference: HTTP methods</h2>
    <table class="routes">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method get">GET</span></td><td data-label="Meaning">Read/fetch data — no changes made.</td></tr>
        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method post">POST</span></td><td data-label="Meaning">Create something new (or, for login, start a session).</td></tr>
        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method patch">PATCH</span></td><td data-label="Meaning">Update part of an existing record.</td></tr>
        <tr><td data-label="Method"><span class="method delete">DELETE</span></td><td data-label="Meaning">Remove a record permanently.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="intro-box">
    <h2>Error responses &amp; rate limits</h2>
    <ul style="margin-bottom:0;">
      <li>Missing or invalid login cookie → <code>404</code> with <code>"no token found"</code> or <code>"invalid token found"</code>.</li>
      <li>Logged in but wrong role for <code>/host</code> routes → <code>401 Access Denied</code>.</li>
      <li>Failed field validation on a create/update route → <code>400</code> or <code>404</code> with an <code>errors</code> object listing every invalid field.</li>
      <li>All <code>/api/v1</code> routes are rate-limited: 20 requests per 5 minutes when unauthenticated, 50 requests per 5 minutes once logged in. Going over returns <code>429 "Too many requests"</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

